<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.3.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00413</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.3.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>a787d87b-def0-4899-a08f-b9e0102bb5d6</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="d6f8070d-51ee-4e35-9188-c3c9a9779198"><problem><para>
      <para>1. Lin is solving this system of equations: </para>
      <para>\( \begin {cases} 6x-5y=34\\3x+2y=8 \end {cases} \)</para>
      <para>She starts by rearranging the second equation to isolate the \(y\) variable: \( y = 4 - 1.5x \). She then substitutes the expression \(4 - 1.5x\) for \( y \) in the first equation, as shown:</para>
      <para> \( 6x-5(4-1.5x)=34 \)\( 6x-20-7.5x=34 \)</para>
      <para>\( -1.5x=54 \)
        \( x=-36 \)</para>
      
      <para>\( y=4-1.5x \)</para>
      <para>\( y=4-1.5 \cdot(-36) \)</para>
      <para>\( y=58 \)</para>
      <para>Does Lin’s solution of \((-36, 58)\) makes both equations in the system true?</para>
    </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>yes; Her solution makes both equations true.</para><para>No; Her solution does not make both equations true.</para></problem><solution><para>No; Her solution does not make both equations true.</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is that Lin’s solution does not make both equations true. </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section>
<para>In 3 - 9, solve the systems of equations by substitution.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="a42eaa70-a2fc-4597-8102-6b37c1b48ad6"><problem><para>
      <para>3. \(\left\{\begin{array}{l}2x+y=-2\\3x-y=7\end{array}\right.\)</para>
    </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((−1,0)\)</para><para>\((0,−2) \)</para><para>\((1,−4)\)</para><para>\((2,6)\)</para></problem><solution><para>\((1,−4)\)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \((1,−4)\).
      </para><para>Check the solution in both equations.</para>
      <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}2x+y&amp;=&amp;-2
        \\ 2(1)+(-4)&amp;=&amp;-2
        \\ 2-4&amp;=&amp;-2
        \\ -2&amp;=&amp;-2\checkmark
        \\ \end{array}\)</para>
      
      <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}3x-y&amp;=&amp;7
        \\ 3(1)-(-4)&amp;=&amp;7
        \\ 3+4&amp;=&amp;7
        \\ 7&amp;=&amp;7\checkmark
        \\ \end{array}\)</para>
      <para>(4,-1) Makes both equations in the system true, therefore it is a solution.</para>
      
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
